From 0000000000000000000000000000000000000000 Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: Jonathan Schwender <schwenderjonathan@gmail.com>
Date: Thu, 8 Oct 2026 15:56:16 +0000
Subject: [PATCH] ohos: Insert committed IME text through a composition update

Since d2abb3339dd (#48690) moved composition handling into
`EditingAction`, a composition end only finishes the composition and the
text is inserted by a composition update. The OpenHarmony port still sent a
commit as an end event alone, so text typed with the soft keyboard no
longer reached the page. Send an update followed by the end, as the
desktop port does since that change.

Meant for upstream; the ArkWeb port had the same problem in its own copy of
this code.

Validation: on a PLR-AL00, servoshell production HAP: tap a text input of a page and type with `uitest uiInput inputText`; the text must appear in the field (it stays empty without this change).
AI-assisted: Yes (agent session; root-caused from the on-device IME failures of the 2026-10-08 sync, written and tested by the agent)
Signed-off-by: Jonathan Schwender <schwenderjonathan@gmail.com>
---
 ports/servoshell/egl/app.rs | 5 +++++
 1 file changed, 5 insertions(+)

diff --git a/ports/servoshell/egl/app.rs b/ports/servoshell/egl/app.rs
index 09051398d38..61b036e934f 100644
--- a/ports/servoshell/egl/app.rs
+++ b/ports/servoshell/egl/app.rs
@@ -642,6 +642,11 @@ impl App {
             KeyState::Down,
             Key::Named(NamedKey::Process),
         )));
+        // Servo inserts the text of a composition update; the end event only finishes it.
+        webview.notify_input_event(InputEvent::Ime(ImeEvent::Composition(CompositionEvent {
+            state: CompositionState::Update,
+            data: text.clone(),
+        })));
         webview.notify_input_event(InputEvent::Ime(ImeEvent::Composition(CompositionEvent {
             state: CompositionState::End,
             data: text,
